---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Move a board or a folder into a folder; / is the root. A folder takes its boards along.
Moving one board needs no -y. Moving a folder with boards reaches everyone who sees them, so it needs -y; without it only the dry run is shown.

USAGE
  holst board mv <board> <folder> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board    The board or folder to move
  folder   The folder to move into: a folder id, link or part of its name; / is the root

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws   Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
  -y, --yes            Confirm a risky change; a terminal asks instead; without one only the dry run is shown (exit code 77)
  -n, --dry-run        Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b mv "Roadmap" "Plans"
  $ holst b mv "Plans" / -y

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
